    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0671" n="659" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg659"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/4–1146: Circular
                    telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic
                        Officers</hi><anchor n="79" xml:id="d495-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-11T14:00:00-05:00">April 11, 1946—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Joint US–USSR Commission Seoul deadlocked Apr 9. US final position: It will not
                    hold dislike of Moscow communiqué (trusteeship) as criterion of acceptability of
                    parties to be consulted in formation provisional govt. USSR final position: It
                    will not speak to or consult with any party which has opposed Moscow
                    communiqué.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d495-f1" n="79" type="source" xml:id="d495-f1-content">
                <p>At Chungking.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
